INT. WEDDING CAKE BAKERY - BACK KITCHEN - DAY

Flour in the air. Sheet pans, piping bags, a six-tier cake in the middle of the floor leaning ever so slightly to the left. A clock says 2:14. The wedding is at 3:00.

CORNELIUS "CORKY" BANKS (50s, head baker, flour-dusted apron) holds his head in his hands. His sous-chef PRIYANKA SHAH-WILLIAMS (30s, hairnet, eyes of steel) circles the cake with a ruler. Their apprentice DESMOND "DEMI" OKORO (teen, oversized chef whites) holds a piping bag like a weapon. And the bride's mother, MRS. VALENTINA CRESPO (60s, hat the size of a hubcap), stands in the doorway with her arms crossed.

CORKY
It's fine. It's totally fine.

PRIYANKA
It's leaning, Corky.

CORKY
Everything leans. The Tower of Pisa leans.

PRIYANKA
The Tower of Pisa isn't going to be eaten by two hundred guests.

MRS. CRESPO
Is something wrong with my daughter's cake?

CORKY
No, Mrs. Crespo.

PRIYANKA
Yes.

CORKY
(to Priyanka)
Stop helping.

DEMI
Chef, I can fix it.

CORKY
No, Demi.

DEMI
With dowels.

PRIYANKA
He's actually right.

CORKY
Demi has never used a dowel in his life.

DEMI
I've used toothpicks.

CORKY
Toothpicks are not dowels.

Mrs. Crespo marches in. She stops at the cake, takes off her hat, puts it on the counter, and rolls her sleeves.

MRS. CRESPO
Show me where the dowels are.

CORKY
Mrs. Crespo, please.

MRS. CRESPO
Cornelius. I raised four children and buried two husbands. I can handle a dowel.

Priyanka hands her a bundle. Corky sits down on a flour sack and puts his head back in his hands. Demi steps in, holds the cake steady with both palms, and braces his feet.

DEMI
Is this how they do it in movies?

PRIYANKA
No.

DEMI
What do they do?

PRIYANKA
They hire a better apprentice.

He grins. She grins back, almost. Mrs. Crespo drives the first dowel through the top three tiers with a surgeon's precision. The cake groans. Settles. Straightens. All four of them hold their breath.

MRS. CRESPO
There.

CORKY
(not looking up)
Is it straight?

PRIYANKA
It's straight.

CORKY
Tell me honestly.

DEMI
It's very straight, Chef.

Corky lifts his head. The cake stands tall and perfect. He lowers his hands, stunned.

CORKY
Mrs. Crespo, I owe you my career.

MRS. CRESPO
You owe me a slice.

PRIYANKA
That's actually the bride's slice.

MRS. CRESPO
Then you owe me two.

The clock ticks to 2:20. Priyanka claps once, sharply.

PRIYANKA
Frosting touch-ups. Demi, the roses. Corky, the transport van.

CORKY
The van is in the shop.

PRIYANKA
You told me it was fixed.

CORKY
I told you it was fixed in my heart.

Silence. Mrs. Crespo lifts her hat from the counter, puts it back on her head, and picks up her car keys.

MRS. CRESPO
I have a station wagon.

CORKY
Mrs. Crespo, it's a six-tier cake.

MRS. CRESPO
Cornelius, I have a very large station wagon.

He looks at her. At the cake. At Priyanka, who shrugs, and at Demi, who is already carrying a tray of roses toward the back door.

CORKY
Fine. We're doing this.

PRIYANKA
We're doing this.

DEMI
We're doing this!

MRS. CRESPO
Somebody open the door.
